# Ignore everything by default
*

# Unignore tracked files
!.gitignore
!README.md
!LICENSE
!criteria.md
!cv_tailoring_prompt.md
!igor_pivnyk_cv_base_updated.tex
!igor_pivnyk_cv_base_updated.pdf
!requirements.txt
!sections.example.py
# Deliberately trackable trusted CODE. Never put credentials or private CV
# values here; keep those in environment variables or a mode-600 .env file.
!job_search_config.py
!job_search_config.example.py
# seen_jobs.json is NOT tracked on main — it lives on the orphan `state` branch.

# Unignore GitHub Actions workflow directory
!.github/
!.github/**

# Unignore the job_search package, the offline characterization suite, and the
# pytest config. Without these, a fresh clone / CI gets ModuleNotFoundError —
# the package files would stay invisible under the `*` default-ignore.
!job_search/
!job_search/**
!tests/
!tests/**
!docs/
!docs/job-search-project-audit-2026-07-15.md
!pyproject.toml

# Unignore the Raspberry Pi deployment doc and setup script (but nothing else
# under docs/, e.g. docs/superpowers/, stays ignored).
!docs/
!docs/deploy-rpi.md
!docs/configuration.md
!scripts/
!scripts/setup-rpi.sh
!scripts/run_pipeline.sh
!scripts/enable-jobspy.sh
!scripts/setup-state-sync.sh
!scripts/telegraph_account.py
!scripts/telegraph_preview.py
!scripts/__init__.py

# The vendored ARMv6 tls-client shared library (vendor/tls-client-armv6.so,
# ~13 MB, cross-built for the Pi's arm1176jzf-s core) is intentionally NOT
# tracked — it stays Pi-local so main carries no platform binary. Covered by the
# top-level `*` ignore; scripts/enable-jobspy.sh expects it already present on
# the Pi (where it was cross-built).

# ...but never track Python bytecode or local scratch state, even though the
# allowlist above otherwise un-ignores everything under the package.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
job_state.json
.pytest_cache/
